✔ a steady trickle that keeps making progress cannot extend the total deadline (200.8227ms)
✔ a client abort during the read ends it at once, cancels, and removes the abort listener (61.759ms)
✔ an already-aborted request is refused without reading and the source is cancelled (1.2286ms)
✔ an over-limit body is refused, the source is cancelled, and the reader is released (1.0717ms)
✔ a body exactly at the cap is accepted (1.0091ms)
✔ a source whose cancel never settles does not hold the reader past the grace period (181.4021ms)
✔ a source whose cancel rejects causes no unhandled rejection, on timeout, over-limit and abort (205.941ms)
✔ a stream that errors mid-read is rethrown after cleanup (44.596ms)
✔ a result already queued behind a blocked thread is a timeout, not ok (data then EOF), with the timer unfired (150.8615ms)
✔ a result already queued behind a blocked thread is a timeout, not ok (zero-byte progress then EOF), with the timer unfired (150.7898ms)
✔ a result already queued behind a blocked thread is a timeout, not ok (EOF only), with the timer unfired (150.6146ms)
✔ a delayed continuation after an earlier client abort keeps the first reason (aborted, not timeout) (150.7226ms)
✔ a body that finishes inside the budget is still ok when the thread is not blocked (0.504ms)
✔ the budget can never be switched off: missing, zero, negative and non-finite values use the configured default (0.8616ms)
✔ many one-byte chunks: bytes are exact and live memory does not grow with the chunk count (3316.3741ms)
